\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Example}
\title{Removing the interior of one strip}
\date{2026-11-27}

\p{At identity links restrict the operator of \ref{fdip-01B6} to one strip, keeping the diagonal terms and dropping both outgoing hops. At #{p=\pm\pi /2} its square still bounds the identity from below. At #{p=0,\pi} the two normal terms before grading have the form #{d\bbI -V} and #{d\bbI -V^\dagger} for the open shift #{V}. In the respective strips #{d} takes values #{2/3,-3/2} at zero momentum and #{8/3,1/2} at #{\pi}. Since #{V^m=0}, each inverse is given by the finite polynomial #{\sum_{j=0}^{m-1}d^{-j-1}V^j} or its adjoint. Both open-strip restrictions are invertible.}
